{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1 exit) — confirmed root cause\n\n**Mechanism (runtime-confirmed):** `_voter_error` (src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:132-148) emits the line-start marker `VOTER_ERROR {json}` on TWO paths: `logger.error(line)` and `print(line, file=sys.stderr)`. `configure_logging()` (src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:129-168, called at import by `rebar.review_bot.app`) attaches a StreamHandler(sys.stdout) with `%(message)s` format to the `rebar` logger, so the logged copy ALSO lands at line start. journald ingests the container's stdout and stderr into ONE stream (`journalctl CONTAINER_NAME=… -o cat`), so the probe's anchored count (infra/scripts/observability.sh:166, `grep -cE '^VOTER_ERROR \\{'`) counts each real error twice — matching the journal evidence (duplicate lines with identical microsecond timestamps: one record, two sinks).\n\n**Runtime experiment (subprocess driving `_voter_error`, counting `^VOTER_ERROR \\{` matches over stdout+stderr = the journald view):**\n- configured logging: stdout=1 stderr=1 → probe_countable=2 (the bug)\n- unconfigured logging: stdout=0 stderr=1 → probe_countable=1 (the fallback works; `lastResort` never fires because `src/rebar/__init__.py:159` installs a NullHandler on the `rebar` logger)\n\n**Rival ruled out:** \"the dual print was double-counting since day one\" — false: before `configure_logging` existed, `logger.error` found only the NullHandler (found>0 → no lastResort), emitted nothing, and the count was correct (observability.sh's own calibration note: \"221 line-start == 221 real\", recorded pre-c130 era anchor fix 8c2f).\n\n**caused_by (date test):** the implicated emitter lines shipped with the marker itself (1d1a072a75c, 2026-06-29, S4b/918c) and predate the transition — they did not cause it. The behavior became wrong when commit b0ac2544720 (2026-07-16, `rebar-ticket: c130-6a87-531e-4441`, irongray-profound-abalone, \"configure logging so structured _emit INFO events reach stdout/journald\") wired the rebar-logger handler, activating the logged copy of a marker that already had an unconditional stderr print. A reviewer of that change could plausibly have caught the double emission of the ERROR-level alarm markers. Class: **regression**. (The S4b commit is the carrier of the fix site, not the origin — divergence from whole-file blame noted deliberately.)\n\n**Legitimacy (authoritative contract):** observability.sh:159-165 documents the anchored count as \"matches every genuine record\" and \"a token is an alarm contract\"; one real error must produce one countable line. Two violates it. Confirmed a defect, not working-as-designed.\n\n**Sibling sweep (Step 7 Axis 1, construct = \"line-start marker string passed to BOTH a logger call and a stderr print\"):**\n- CONFIRMED `MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR` — voter_merge.py `merge_change_error` (logger.error + print), anchored-counted at observability.sh:196 → live doubling of review_bot_merge_change_errors.\n- CONFIRMED `RECONCILE_DEGRADED` — reconcile.py `_degraded` (logger.warning + print; docstring: \"Mirrors voter's VOTER_ERROR marker convention\") → doubled line-start marker in journald (no anchored counter today; latent for any future probe).\n- CONFIRMED `ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR` — artifact_emit.py `_artifact_emit_error` (logger.warning + print) → same latent doubling.\n- CLEAN `AUTODEPLOY_*` — autodeploy.sh `marker()` prints once to stderr; no logger path; not affected.\n\n**Fix shape (per the ticket's preferred candidate — emitter-side single line-start emission):** keep the unconditional `print(line, file=sys.stderr)` as the ONE line-start marker emission (it is the fail-safe and works in both configured and misconfigured logging), and change the logger copy to log the structured record body (`json.dumps(record)`) WITHOUT the token prefix — same shape `_emit` already logs — so the log-stream copy stays for operators/caplog but can never match `^TOKEN \\{`. Applied to all four confirmed sites. Structural class guard test prevents new markers reintroducing the construct."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787419112063233001,"uuid":"86cf5590-f0fd-4702-9763-62ddfa178de1"}